"<thinking>\n\nStep A: Text Breakdown\n\n1. \"We are currently developing a mobile football app that will be available for Android and iOS devices.\"\n2. \"It is particularly important to us that the app runs quickly and smoothly so that it is fully loaded and ready to use within a maximum of two seconds after starting.\"\n3. \"With our app, we want to offer football fans a central platform where they can stay comprehensively informed at all times.\"\n4. \"To achieve this, users can display current football news of their favorite teams and also select preferred sports channels individually.\"\n5. \"In addition to the news, users can follow the results of their favorite teams live via a live ticker.\"\n6. \"Our app will offer extensive coverage of all leagues and competitions, both national and international.\"\n7. \"Detailed team and player information will also be available at any time.\"\n8. \"Another highlight is the integration of live stream links, for example, from providers such as DAZN or Sky Sport.\"\n9. \"These are available directly in the app as soon as the live broadcast has begun.\"\n10. \"Of course, it is ensured that compliance with transmission rights is maintained. Live streams will only be displayed when the respective rights are fulfilled in the country.\"\n11. \"The LiveFootball app should also give users the option to retrieve the live results of their favorite teams in real time.\"\n12. \"To implement this function, the app includes an integrated live ticker module that enables the retrieval and display of live data in real time.\"\n13. \"The user interface is designed so that users can access the information in the app directly.\"\n14. \"The user interface is a key component of the app and connects various modules that are displayed together and managed via the interface.\"\n15. \"The live ticker module communicates directly via the interface with the user interface to display and continuously update current match data.\"\n16. \"The live data is retrieved via an API from an external server. The server is located outside the app and provides the data dynamically so that the live ticker module can access it flexibly.\"\n17. \"In addition to the live ticker module, the app also offers additional modules that allow users to individually configure the app and connect their own interface to the user interface.\"\n18. \"Furthermore, the app is linked to a notification system that provides users with information about current events as soon as the notification function is activated.\"\n19. \"All modules and the user interface are fixed components of the app and remain consistent even with external server updates.\"\n20. \"Registration and login are designed to be uncomplicated and can be completed directly at app startup.\"\n21. \"Users have the option to personalize their experience by following favorite clubs and receiving notifications about news or results of their favorite teams.\"\n22. \"In addition, users can share news and game reports via social media directly from the app.\"\n23. \"We are aware that many mobile apps have to operate under difficult conditions. Therefore, the app is developed so that it functions reliably even with limited network coverage.\"\n24. \"The app remains usable offline, even if it temporarily loses connection.\"\n25. \"On match days with a particularly high number of accesses, our app is designed so that up to 100,000 users can be served simultaneously without performance loss.\"\n26. \"To prevent technical problems, the app goes through a thorough testing and support process before release to detect and resolve any malfunctions early.\"\n27. \"In addition, user feedback and app reviews are continuously evaluated to improve functionality.\"\n28. \"Data protection is our highest priority. All personal data of users are processed in compliance with the GDPR.\"\n\nStep B: Requirement Extraction & Sorting\n\nFunctional (FR):\n- App must be available on Android and iOS (1)\n- Users can display current football news of favorite teams (4)\n- Users can select preferred sports channels (4)\n- Users can follow results of favorite teams live via a live ticker (5)\n- App covers all leagues and competitions, national/international (6)\n- Display detailed team and player info (7)\n- Integration of live stream links from providers (8)\n- Live stream links appear when the broadcast begins (9)\n- Live streams only shown when rights are allowed in country (10)\n- Retrieve live results in real time (11)\n- Integrated live ticker module for live data retrieval/display (12)\n- User interface provides direct access to info (13)\n- Modules connect to UI and are managed via UI (14)\n- Live ticker module updates match data continuously via UI (15)\n- Live ticker gets live data via external API (16)\n- Additional modules allow individual app configuration/connection to UI (17)\n- Notification system informs users of events when enabled (18)\n- Registration and login are simple and available at startup (20)\n- Users can follow favorite clubs and get notifications for them (21)\n- Share news/game reports on social media (22)\n\nNon-Functional (NFR):\n- Runs quickly and smoothly, loads fully within max 2s (2)\n- Modules/ui are consistent even if the server changes (19)\n- App functions reliably in limited network (23)\n- App remains usable offline if connection lost (24)\n- Serves up to 100,000 users simultaneously without performance loss (25)\n- Goes through thorough testing and support before release (26)\n- User feedback/review is continuously evaluated (27)\n- All data GDPR compliant (28)\n\nStep C: De-duplication & Overlap Check\n\n- Multiple points discuss news/team/channel selection: Consolidate into one requirement about customizable feeds (FR-002).\n- Live ticker/real-time/live results/live data retrieval: Roll into requirements about live ticker module and real-time results (FR-005).\n- Registration/login/personalization: Separate requirements for registration, following teams, notification (FR-010, FR-011, FR-012).\n- Social share is unique.\n- Consistency of modules and UI (even with server updates) is clear (NFR-002).\n- Performance, offline, scalability, reliability, GDPR all unique (NFR-001, NFR-003, NFR-004, NFR-005, NFR-006).\n\nStep D: BDD Planning\n\nFR-001: (Availability)\nGiven I am a user with a compatible device\nWhen I search for the app in the Play or App Store\nThen I can find and download the app for both Android and iOS\n\nFR-002: (Custom news and channels)\nGiven I'm on the news screen\nWhen I select my favorite club and channel\nThen I see a news feed tailored to my choice\n\nFR-003: (Live ticker)\nGiven I've added a favorite team\nWhen a live match is ongoing\nThen I see real-time scores via the live ticker\n\nFR-004: (Coverage)\nGiven I access results\nWhen I select any major league or competition\nThen I see information for both national and international events\n\nFR-005: (Team/Player info)\nGiven I search for a team or player\nWhen I select their page\nThen I see stats and detailed info\n\nFR-006: (Live stream links)\nGiven a live match with broadcast rights\nWhen the broadcast begins\nThen I see a live stream link for the provider\n\nFR-007: (Transmission rights)\nGiven my country fulfills the streaming right\nWhen I view live matches\nThen only available streams are shown\n\nFR-008: (Notification system)\nGiven I enable notifications\nWhen an event occurs\nThen I get a push message\n\nFR-009: (Social Sharing)\nGiven I'm reading an article\nWhen I click share\nThen I can post to social media\n\nFR-010: (Registration/Login)\nGiven it's my first app launch\nWhen I enter my credentials\nThen I complete signup or login simply\n\nFR-011: (Personalization)\nGiven I want to personalize\nWhen I follow clubs\nThen my feed and notifications are adjusted accordingly\n\nNFR-001: (Performance)\nGiven user launches app\nWhen fully loaded\nThen startup occurs within 2s\n\nNFR-002: (Module/UI Consistency)\nGiven server is updated\nWhen I use the app\nThen core modules and UI remain consistent\n\nNFR-003: (Network reliability)\nGiven connection is weak\nWhen I access features\nThen critical functionality operates\n\nNFR-004: (Offline mode)\nGiven my connection drops\nWhen I continue using the app\nThen previously accessed data stays usable\n\nNFR-005: (Scale)\nGiven it's match day with 100k+ concurrent users\nWhen I use the app\nThen performance is not degraded\n\nNFR-006: (Testing and Quality)\nGiven app is due for release\nWhen it passes QA and support checks\nThen no known defects exist\n\nNFR-007: (GDPR Compliance)\nGiven I use the app\nWhen my personal data is processed\nThen it happens according to GDPR rules\n\nStep E: ID Assignment\n\nAssign sequential FR-001 to FR-012 and NFR-001 to NFR-007\n\n</thinking>"